  "drawnOn": "B39M",
  "description": "Fuselage: Alaska's standard white with the lime/Atlas-blue/midnight sweep behind the wing, the Atlas blue reaching forward along the belly to under the engine. Cheatlines: None. Tail: Standard midnight-blue fin with the Alaska Native man's face. Engines: Standard. Winglets: Standard. Titles: The standard midnight 'Alaska' forward; 'MARINERS' big in the team's navy lettering with a teal outline from over the wing to the sweep. Artwork: Mariner Moose waving between the two titles, the Mariners compass-rose logo at the end of 'MARINERS', and 'fly, fly away' (Dave Niehaus's home-run call) in small type. Colors hex: Mariners navy and teal from the team; the paint matched by eye.",
