  "notes": "Drawn from Alaska's photo of the left side; the right side (two 2026 Commons photos) carries the same layout. The rest of the scheme is Alaska's standard (ASA/standard), whose sweep, fin, engines and winglets are copied. Re-checked 2026-11-15 (drawn on the 737-9): titles' lengths kept (measured on Alaska's side-on photo); 'Alaska' lowercase about 0.55 of its A. The Atlas-blue swoosh and the standard's aft sweep made smooth curves (the swoosh's pointed aft tip kept a corner), with the silver-grey stripe ahead of the lime that the standard now has.",
  "from": "2024-09",
